From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] dirstat: use APFS's directory statistics only with its header

dirstat.c asks APFS for directory sizes through apfs/apfs_fsctl.h, which
Apple doesn't publish (APFS is closed). Without the header, take the path
the simulator takes: the portable fallback that walks the directory, which
dirstatat_np forces today anyway (rdar://32794924).

Rebase-risk: low (one condition).
---
diff --git a/libdarwin/dirstat.c b/libdarwin/dirstat.c
--- a/libdarwin/dirstat.c
+++ b/libdarwin/dirstat.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 #include "dirstat.h"
 #include "dirstat_collection.h"
 
-#if !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR
+#if !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR && __has_include(<apfs/apfs_fsctl.h>)
 #define HAS_APFS
 #endif
 
